# One normalization rule for every platform.
#
# `rustfmt.toml` pins `newline_style = "Unix"`, while a Windows checkout defaults
# to git's `core.autocrlf=true` — which rewrites every text file to CRLF, so
# `cargo fmt --check` fails on the Windows CI runner before the build starts.
# Forcing LF at checkout makes formatting platform-independent; existing clones
# on Windows need a one-off `git add --renormalize .` after pulling this file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never normalize binary assets.
*.bin binary
